# The original A₅ source consumers

The nonabelian recognition in Section 13.5 supplies the abelian point
closure used in Section 13.6. The terminal source exports retain their
stated earlier classification and centralizer inputs; this umbrella does
not assert their discharge or the complete Theorem 13.6.1.

The normalized terminal branch also consumes the original full-quotient/MS
selection through the action-only nonblock contradiction, without a strict
secondary-core-enlargement input. Its genuine MS selection, Cartan escape and
ambient completion recognition remain explicit earlier-source premises.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, Section 13.6, printed pp.926–935.
